We decided to primarily build part of the robot's chassis in 3D, as we wanted to design it to our liking. 
We wanted to structure each element of our robot in a more organized way, so we made our circuit board in 3D.

Another idea we had at the beginning was to make our robot's base out of methacrylate, cutting it with a laser printer. 
In the end, it didn't turn out as we expected, so we discarded it.

We also decided to design the sensors ourselves. In the end, it was easier to design and test them than to buy something online. 
We designed them in Tinkercad and then sent them to be printed, always in black to maintain the aesthetic.
Being able to use a 3D printer for all the ideas we've come up with has been fantastic.
